Cron Jobs

Cron is a Linux scheduling service used to automatically execute tasks at specified times.

Examples:

Daily backups
Log cleanup
Running maintenance scripts
Scheduled system tasks
Command
crontab -e

Purpose:

Edit the current user's scheduled Cron Jobs.

Example
0 2 * * * backup.sh

Meaning:

Run the backup script every day at 2:00 AM.

Why Cron Jobs Are Useful
Automates repetitive tasks
Reduces manual work
Ensures regular system maintenance
Improves system reliability
